{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-retrofit-county",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.84: the `nr-retrofit-county` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its user input database's NONROAD RETROFIT programs -- Washtenaw County, Michigan, August 2020, weekday, the Industrial sector's NONROAD diesel (fuel 23), THC, CO, NOx, methane, SO2, NMHC, VOC, PM10 and PM2.5 running exhaust. Its twin `nr-retrofit-county-base` is the same RunSpec without the programs.\n\nIT CHECKS `rtf_reduction`. MOVES writes the sixteen nrRetrofitFactors records as NONROAD's /RETROFIT/ packet, and NONROAD skips three (a retrofit year after 2020, a model year after 2020, an SCC the run does not request) and reduces exhaust HC, CO and NOx per (SCC, hp, model year, technology) by the capped fraction retrofitted times the effectiveness, summed over retrofit IDs and capped. 255 of the 1,881 cells move -- THC, CO, NOx and, through MOVES's speciation of the reduced THC, methane, NMHC and VOC; SO2, PM10 and PM2.5 do not -- and every cell reproduces, key-exact, no `cell_exception`. `run_retrofitUnported` reads 0."
  },
